                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm usually not a big RPG player myself, but so far the little time I put into this game has been great.\n\nAs with most old-school RPGs the mechanics are pretty simple, but the writing and the omnipresent humour really make this game enjoyable. Some dialogues are downright hilariously unexpected and I've laughed quite a few times because of that. \n\nOverall the atmosphere really comes together with the music. It's surprisingly well written and sometimes catchy.\n\nFor the price and for what's advertised I really don't have anything negative to say about it. My only gripe is that I'm bad at finding the right answers to move on in quests, but that really comes down to me being crappy at RPGs.",
